{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Who appointed you a man.</b> Why, you are still a lad." "<b>Are you saying to kill me.</b> From here we learn that he killed him by the Explicit Name (Exodus Rabbah 1)." "<b>And Moshe feared.</b> As its plain sense. And its midrash: he was troubled over seeing in Israel wicked informers; he said: now perhaps they are not worthy of being redeemed (Exodus Rabbah 1)." "<b>Indeed the thing is known.</b> As its meaning. And its midrash: the thing has become known to me that I had wondered at — what did Israel sin, of all seventy nations, to be subjugated in crushing labor? But now I see that they are worthy of this (Exodus Rabbah 1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:16.778044653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}